hey're breaking in, and before someone's security alarm can go off before the police can show up. They're in and out, and they've robbed you blind. they move on to the next house. It's only a matter of time before a mom, comes home from the grocery store with her little ones, and walks into her home and is face to face with these people. I don't want to see another American die at the hands of someone here illegally. It breaks my heart. I imagine myself being in that position, where I walk in, my arms full of groceries, and my children next to me, helping me carry in the groceries, and there's a bunch of gang members breaking into our home. This is happening in Arizona right now. That piece of garbage legislation would have done nothing to stop that. Actually, it would continue to make it happen. I want to talk with you about abortion. I know it's on the minds of people. It's looking like that petition will end up making it onto the ballot this year, and it will be the Constitutional Amendment in November. How has that impacted your campaigning this year with it being on so many minds? I don't know that it really has. I mean, I've stayed in my position clearly. I want to help as many women. I am a woman. I care about women's health. I care about women in general. I'm the youngest of nine. We have eight girls in our family. I have a daughter, so I care deeply. I just want to make sure that women have more options, so they're making a healthier choice. And I want to save as many babies as possible. But guess what? I'm running for U.S. Senate. That is not something that I have a saying, other than a vote. I'm running for U.S. Senate, and I have said I would not pass or introduce or vote for a federal abortion ban. I believe we fought to push this back to the state level. And what I want to see is more women to be able to feel that they can have a baby and take care of it. If you ask your mom, or your cameraman's mom, or any mom watching, what is the greatest achievement, joy, accomplishment in her life, the things she's most proud of. If you ask any mother, watching this, she'll say it's being a mother. I just want women to have that option, to know that that is a true option, they can attain that. And I don't want when they're at this low point or tragic, difficult point. They walk into an abortion clinic to only have one choice. And frankly, that's what they're given, one choice. There's help out there, and I want them to know about that. And so I'm gonna do whatever I can. In the U.S. Senate to make sure that, you know, we're supporting families. Republicans, for a long time, have talked a lot about being pro life, but they haven't been necessarily working to say, we're pro family. And so once you do bring that beautiful life into the world, how are we helping to support you so that that family can strengthen and grow? Our country is only as strong as the most important institution. And the most important institution is the family, and the family is struggling right now, in many cases, crumbling. And families that are keeping it together are struggling because of democrat policies when it comes to their dismal economic policies, making it where mom and dad have to get two jobs, and then maybe they have to, you know, drive Uber Eats at night. I want you to have one job and be able to be with your family. I want you to be able to make a living and not have to be, you know, once you bring a family into the world, having to work two and three jobs. So I want to do things in D.C. to help so that families can grow, flourish, and then our country grows. You approach this issue. When you talk about this. Even right now, you talk about this as an issue about the mother and the child and the family. We know, you're a mother, that when that nine months is over, that is not the end. That's just the beginning. So what is your plan to support birth and support children after they're born? I think I want to see a cultural shift where we see 