al. That wasn't the problem. I mean, the my policies were phenomenal. My policies are putting America first. And that means making for a strong border, a strong economy, schools that are actually teaching a really good world class education, including trade skill training and career training right there in high school, so that our kids are getting out of high school, ready to take on jobs that are out there. Not saying, okay, I don't have any ability right now. I need to go out and learn another skill. And so my policies already appealed to Republicans, Democrats, independence. That's the beauty of America first. You didn't have to love President Trump to say, wow, the economy was doing better. Unemployment rates were low in every sector, no matter what your skin color was or your background. That's what we're going to get back to. So my policies appeal to all Arizonans, and I'm going to continue to tell people that we do have the ability to solve these problems. This is not, I know, I'm not alone when I wake up in the middle of the night, and maybe you do, too, and say, ooh, what's gonna happen tomorrow? The world seems to be out of control. America's got so many problems. But I also know that when we get together, we come together, not just as Republicans, I don't want just Republicans solving the problems. I want Americans solving the problems. When we come together, and we put common sense solutions, set forth common sense solutions, we can solve these problems, and do so quickly. I've always been reaching out to all Republicans. I've always been reaching out to independents. I was just in the airport, and I met a great man, and he said, I'm a Hispanic Democrat, and I voted for you, and I'm gonna vote for you again. And so we're bringing people together. I don't pay attention to what the media's saying. They want to act like, oh, my gosh, there's no unity. There's a ton of unity in America right now. I'm a national name right now, and I understand, wherever I go